le its own docstring lists. I added `Book(\"Emma\", \"Austen\", 1815, 1)`; the author, year and copy count match the search tests.\n3. **`catalog/fees.py`**: `late_fee` added the daily fee to the day count instead of multiplying. It's now `days_late * DAILY_FEE`.\n4. **`catalog/inventory.py`**: `recent(n)` returned one event too many (`[-n - 1:]`). It now returns `[-n:]`, and an empty list when `n <= 0`, since `[-0:]` would return the whole history.\n5. **`catalog/members.py`**: `MAX_BORROWED` was 3, but the comment above it and the tests both say five. I set it to 5.\n6. **`catalog/search.py`**: it imported `normalize` from `catalog.nonexistent`, which doesn't exist. It now imports it from `catalog.text`.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "run_id": "opencode:make-ci-green:claude-opus-5-5:trial2", "sampling_observed": null, "score": 1.0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 17.503, "t_checker_s": 0.228, "t_env_setup_s": 0.002, "task": "make-ci-green", "timeout_s": 840, "token_basis": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1262, "tokens_cache_read": 54097, "tokens_cache_write": 17502, "tokens_fresh": 1262, "tokens_input_uncached": 10, "tokens_output": 1252, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 54097, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 17502, "tokens_proxy_calls": 5, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 777, "tokens_proxy_output": 1267, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": null, "tokens_reasoning": 0, "toolchain": {"ai": "5.0.97", "anthropic": "2.0.0", "bun": "1.3.3"}, "trial": 2, "ts_iso": "2026-10-05T17:05:24", "turns": 4, "usage_raw": [{"cache": {"read": 11754, "write": 2847}, "input": 4, "output": 128, "reasoning": 0}, {"cache": {"read": 11754, "write": 4234}, "input": 2, "output": 151, "reasoning": 0}, {"cache": {"read": 14601, "write": 5656}, "input": 2, "output": 473, "reasoning": 0}, {"cache": {"read": 15988, "write": 4765}, "input": 2, "output": 500, "reasoning": 0}], "version_drift": true, "wall_time_s": 17.503, "workspace_changed": true, "